Test only: never skip the bind conflict check in inet_csk_get_port().

Both bind caches (tb->fastreuse and tb->fastreuseport) are ignored, so
every bind() and listen() to a named port takes the full check. The
results of this kernel are the reference the other kernels are compared
against. SK_FORCE_REUSE (TCP_REPAIR) still skips the check, as it is not
a cache.

---
diff --git a/net/ipv4/inet_connection_sock.c b/net/ipv4/inet_connection_sock.c
index e56beec43877..0fa7b6b72c98 100644
--- a/net/ipv4/inet_connection_sock.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/inet_connection_sock.c
@@ -544,8 +544,8 @@ int inet_csk_get_port(struct sock *sk, unsigned short snum)
 	if (!found_port) {
 		if (!hlist_empty(&tb->bhash2)) {
 			if (sk->sk_reuse == SK_FORCE_REUSE ||
-			    (tb->fastreuse > 0 && reuse) ||
-			    sk_reuseport_match(tb, sk))
+			    (false && ((tb->fastreuse > 0 && reuse) ||
+				       sk_reuseport_match(tb, sk))))
 				check_bind_conflict = false;
 		}
 
